configure: do not treat missing x86 intrinsics support as fatal

The darwin cross toolchain uses clang 6.0.1, whose <immintrin.h> does
not declare the full intrinsics set exercised by the x86intrin config
test (e.g. _rdseed32_step), so QT_FEATURE_x86intrin evaluates to OFF.
Qt then adds a fatal ERROR report entry whose message embeds the raw
compiler output; the parentheses/quotes in that output additionally
break qt_configure_process_add_report_entry argument re-parsing
("Unknown arguments: ("). Downgrade the entry to a WARNING with a
static message so configure completes and Qt simply builds without
SSE/AVX code paths.

--- a/qtbase/configure.cmake
+++ b/qtbase/configure.cmake
@@ -1278,18 +1278,11 @@
 ]=]
         )
     else()
-        string(CONCAT error_message
-            "x86 intrinsics support missing. Check your compiler settings.\n"
-            "If this is an error, report at https://bugreports.qt.io with your compiler ID and "
-            "version, and this output:\n"
-            "\n"
-            "${TEST_x86intrin_OUTPUT}"
-        )
         qt_configure_add_report_entry(
-            TYPE ERROR
+            TYPE WARNING
             CONDITION (NOT QT_FEATURE_x86intrin)
-            MESSAGE "${error_message}"
+            MESSAGE "x86 intrinsics support missing; building without SSE/AVX code paths. See config.tests/x86intrin for details."
         )
     endif()
 endif()
 qt_configure_add_report_entry(
